  data: {
    LLM: "Don't pay for cards that only marginally improve your hand's strength. Buying a '4' to make a pair is rarely worth 2 units.\n\nThe 'Open Market' read: Watch what your opponents buy. If someone buys a face-up 10 and they already have a 10 showing, you know they have at least three of a kind.\n\nValue Betting the Market: If you have a strong hand, use the buying rounds to build the pot size without looking aggressive. The chips you pay to the market grow the pot for when you eventually win at showdown.",
    Player: "Don't pay for cards that only marginally improve your hand's strength. Buying a '4' to make a pair is rarely worth 2 units.\n\nThe 'Open Market' read: Watch what your opponents buy. If someone buys a face-up 10 and they already have a 10 showing, you know they have at least three of a kind.\n\nValue Betting the Market: If you have a strong hand, use the buying rounds to build the pot size without looking aggressive. The chips you pay to the market grow the pot for when you eventually win at showdown.",
